course: dictionary
lesson: 2640
title: Detain: hold, delay or punish
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Detain means to keep someone in one place so they cannot leave. Context shows which kind of keeping is meant. «The police detained the suspect for questions.» The police would not hold someone just for fun, so detain must mean holding them so they cannot go.
explain: In polite talk, detain means to delay someone. «I won't detain you long» means I won't keep you waiting or stop you for long. The sentence is kind, so detain is not about locking anyone up.
explain: At school, a detention is time kept back after lessons as a punishment. The noun detention comes from the verb detain. To check any meaning, swap in keep or hold and see whether the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Detain means to keep someone in a place and not let them leave.
fact: «Passengers were detained for questioning» means they were held so officials could ask them questions.
fact: «I won't detain you» is a polite way of saying I won't keep you long.
fact: At school, a detention is time kept back after lessons as a punishment.
fact: «Detained at His Majesty's pleasure» is a British legal phrase meaning held in prison for an unknown length of time, with no end date fixed in advance.
exercise: «The police detained the suspect for questions.» What does detained mean? | Set free with a warning | Given a gift | Chased down the street | *Kept in one place and not allowed to leave
exercise: «I won't detain you for long, so sit down.» What does detain mean here? | Carry you off | Bring you a drink | *Keep you for a short time | Stop you from ever speaking
exercise: Nadia got a detention for being late. What is a detention? | A type of school bag | *Time kept back after school as a punishment | A reward for good work | A trip to the park
test: «Detained at His Majesty's pleasure» means held in prison for how long? | *An unknown time, with no end date fixed in advance | A single day | A fixed number of years | Until breakfast
test: Which word is the noun form of detain? | *detention | detail | detect | detour
exam: «The guards detained the visitors until the alarm was checked.» What does detained mean? | Thanked | *Held back and kept from leaving | Welcomed | Sent home quickly
